{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117511","id":3409500043,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7LONeL","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117511","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117511.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117511.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117511","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117511/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117511/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117511/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/64f7bbbf12f76f78999d9b2bad12346d2d8885a4","number":117511,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Improve thread-safety of `Object` signals","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #117396.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> I would recommend looking at these changes with whitespace changes hidden, as there's a fair bit of indentation changes.\r\n\r\nAs mentioned in #117396, interacting with signal connections across multiple threads is not currently thread-safe, despite [claims](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a8e37fc01048823f639c4011af645d2e8e2b79d3/doc/classes/Object.xml#L534) to the contrary. `Object::signal_mutex` is mostly covering `this->signal_map`, but does not cover `target->connections` at all.\r\n\r\nThis fixes that by replacing the `OBJ_SIGNAL_LOCK` macro and `_ObjectSignalLock` struct with a new `ObjectSignalLock` struct that optionally takes two objects instead of just one. This lets us lock the `signal_mutex` of both objects at the same time, and (more importantly) in the same order every time. The latter is done by simply \"sorting\" the mutexes by their memory address, since that should be stable for the lifetime of the object.\r\n\r\nMost of these changes were fairly simple and mechanical in places were we already had the two objects readily available, but a few were less obvious, so are worth elaborating:\r\n\r\n1. `Object::~Object`\r\n    - The scope of the lock when erasing incoming connections has been shrunk to only cover `target->connections`, since we need to lock the `target` mutex. This is technically less thread-safe, since `signal_map` isn't being covered properly, but frankly anything reading/mutating an `Object` currently being destroyed is problematic on so many more levels that this is a non-issue in practice.\r\n    - There was a null check of `c.callable.get_object()` happening during the erasing of outgoing connections, which will always be `this`, so was removed.\r\n2. `Object::_disconnect`\r\n    - There was a null check of `slot->cE` happening before, which is already being done inside of `target_object->connections.erase`, so was removed.\r\n3. `Object::emit_signalp`\r\n    - The scope of the lock has been shrunk to only cover `signal_map` and not the one-shot disconnections. This would otherwise break the lock ordering, since `_disconnect` will internally try to lock both mutexes, but one of them would have (arbitrarily) already been locked.\r\n4. `Object::_remove_user_signal`\r\n    - Since we can't iterate our signal slots while also doing the double-locking, this method needs to be a two-phase thing. We do this by first (under a `this` lock) finding the `slot_map` of the signal, moving it out into a temporary, then erasing it. Then as a second phase we iterate over our now erased `slot_map` and double-lock as per usual.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n*Disclaimer: AI tooling was used in the planning and review of this change, as well as some minor edits. Any code not physically typed out by myself has been carefully reviewed to the best of my ability.*","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","description":"","color":"885544","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","fo